From b3a2bf8c0b23c332ba03ee7300aaa22a4c0a1023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/27] tests: mdb_prefetch_overflow on a generated environment
 of large values

A table of 200 values of 10,000 bytes (three 4 KB overflow pages each), a
table of small values, and a DUPSORT table. The tests read the page cache
through mincore() on the environment's own map.

- Its arguments: 0 for a large value and for a value in a leaf;
  MDB_NOTFOUND for a missing key; EINVAL for the DUPSORT table and for a
  NULL key. In a write transaction, 0 for a value the transaction wrote
  itself, and the value reads back as written.
- After the whole file is dropped from the page cache, it is called for
  every other value. Within 5 s, all of their first pages are in the page
  cache, and at most 10% of the other values' first pages. Every value then
  reads back intact.

The residency test skips where LMDB's page size is not the OS's, and where
the file system does not let pages go (tmpfs). Checked against a broken
version that never calls madvise(): the residency test fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
